          "tz": 60
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Cyril Bordage",
          "email": "cbordage@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-20 22:59:40.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "subject": "LU-20000 lnet: fix per-NI import and tunables warning",
        "message": "LU-20000 lnet: fix per-NI import and tunables warning\n\nSince each NI of a 'net:' block is configured on its own,\nhandle_yaml_config_ni() has a few problems:\n- \"interfaces\" is found with cYAML_get_object_item(), which also\n  searches the next NIs. An NI without \"interfaces\" takes the\n  interfaces of the next NI, which is then added twice, and the\n  import fails with -EEXIST.\n- An NI without \"interfaces\" (e.g. GNILND) is skipped and the\n  import still reports success. Before, it was configured.\n- If conns_per_peer of an NI is invalid, the interfaces already\n  copied to nw_intflist are leaked.\n\nUse cYAML_get_object_child() for \"interfaces\", configure an NI\neven without interfaces, and validate conns_per_peer before the\ninterfaces are copied.\n\nAlso, in lnet_startup_lndnet(), the \"All tunables of NIs of a net\nshould be the same\" warning compares the requested tunables with\nthe ones of the existing net, which were filled in by the LND.\nUnset values are -1, so the warning is printed when adding a\nsecond NI to a net even without tunables. Only compare the values\nset by the user, and print the net and the values.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nFixes: 18bc6c4a5478 (\"LU-20000 lnetctl: bad CPTs/tunables during import\")\nSigned-off-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: Augment:claude-opus-5-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I40168b5cd6305517f17904d86845be39c3514666\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
